00:25:34.175 --> 00:25:36.926
My people were angry.

00:25:36.986 --> 00:25:39.418
I had to go away.

00:25:39.478 --> 00:25:44.039
I ran away and lived with the Mohawks.

00:25:44.100 --> 00:25:48.155
Then the war started, said Magua.

00:25:48.216 --> 00:25:52.902
The French and the English were fighting each other.

00:25:52.962 --> 00:25:56.554
The Mohawks were fighting for the English.

00:25:56.615 --> 00:26:00.446
The Hurons were fighting for the French.

00:26:00.506 --> 00:26:04.228
I was fighting my own people.

00:26:04.288 --> 00:26:08.880
Your father, Monroe, was our chief.

00:26:08.941 --> 00:26:13.443
He told the Mohawks, do not drink brandy.

00:26:13.503 --> 00:26:17.530
But a white man gave me brandy.

00:26:17.590 --> 00:26:19.756
What did Monroe do?

00:26:19.816 --> 00:26:22.268
He gave orders to his men.

00:26:22.328 --> 00:26:27.320
They tied me with ropes, and they beat me.

00:26:27.380 --> 00:26:30.672
I will never forget.

00:26:30.732 --> 00:26:35.134
But, said Cora, woman, shouted Magua.

00:26:35.194 --> 00:26:36.736
He stood up quickly.

00:26:36.796 --> 00:26:39.597
You will be my wife.

00:26:39.657 --> 00:26:43.550
Your sister will go to Fort William Henry.

00:26:43.610 --> 00:26:46.813
She must tell Monroe everything.

00:26:46.873 --> 00:26:49.156
Then Manro will know.

00:26:49.216 --> 00:26:53.447
His daughter lives with me, Magua.

00:26:53.507 --> 00:26:55.668
Never, said Cora.

00:26:55.728 --> 00:26:57.968
I will not be your wife."

00:26:58.028 --> 00:26:59.839
